## 5-3 Construct a query that returns all addresses that are in the same city. You will need to
join the address table to itself, and each row should include two different addresses.

### Solution
In this case, the usage of table alias is necessary, because of the self-join. 
mysql> SELECT a1.address, a2.address, a1.city_id
    -> FROM address a1
    -> INNER JOIN address a2
    -> ON a1.city_id = a2.city_id
    -> AND a1.address_id < a2.address_id;
